ARM: dts: omap5: add the ipu and dsp nodes

The SoC-level description of the two remote processors, taken verbatim
from v5.9 arch/arm/boot/dts/omap5.dtsi, where it was added alongside the
driver rework.  Both are left status = "disabled"; a board turns on what
it has firmware for.

This applies cleanly because the surrounding text has not moved.  The
target-module@55082000 block that the new nodes sit after, and the
dmm@4e000000 block they sit before, are byte-identical between this tree
and v5.9.

Everything the two nodes reference already exists here, which is why
this is two nodes and not a subsystem:

  mmu_ipu, mmu_dsp   already in omap5.dtsi and omap5-l4.dtsi, and both
                     already probe -- /sys/class/iommu on a running Pyra
                     lists 55082000.mmu and 4a066000.mmu
  mailbox            already in omap5-l4.dtsi, with the mbox_ipu and
                     mbox_dsp sub-nodes these point at
  prm_core, prm_dsp  already reset providers; target-module@55082000
                     next door already uses <&prm_core 2>
  scm_conf           already the syscon the dsp boot register lives in
  ipu_clkctrl,
  dsp_clkctrl        already clock providers

The firmware-name strings are upstream's and are the names the build in
experiments/m4-ipu/README.md produces.  Nothing loads until somebody
writes to the remoteproc sysfs state file, so a kernel carrying this
with no firmware installed behaves as it does today.

Origin: v5.9 arch/arm/boot/dts/omap5.dtsi, GPL-2.0-only.
See docs/m4-ipu.md.

--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/omap5.dtsi	2026-09-20 14:06:13.724952665 -0400
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/omap5.dtsi	2026-09-20 14:06:13.778101154 -0400
@@ -216,6 +216,29 @@
 			};
 		};
 
+		dsp: dsp {
+			compatible = "ti,omap5-dsp";
+			ti,bootreg = <&scm_conf 0x304 0>;
+			iommus = <&mmu_dsp>;
+			resets = <&prm_dsp 0>;
+			clocks = <&dsp_clkctrl OMAP5_MMU_DSP_CLKCTRL 0>;
+			firmware-name = "omap5-dsp-fw.xe64T";
+			mboxes = <&mailbox &mbox_dsp>;
+			status = "disabled";
+		};
+
+		ipu: ipu@55020000 {
+			compatible = "ti,omap5-ipu";
+			reg = <0x55020000 0x10000>;
+			reg-names = "l2ram";
+			iommus = <&mmu_ipu>;
+			resets = <&prm_core 0>, <&prm_core 1>;
+			clocks = <&ipu_clkctrl OMAP5_MMU_IPU_CLKCTRL 0>;
+			firmware-name = "omap5-ipu-fw.xem4";
+			mboxes = <&mailbox &mbox_ipu>;
+			status = "disabled";
+		};
+
 		dmm@4e000000 {
 			compatible = "ti,omap5-dmm";
 			reg = <0x4e000000 0x800>;
